=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ VUPDATE @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt VUPDATE @VERSION@ for OpenVMS (vms-vupdate): updates and patches from the VSI Service Platform, early test
1 'NOTICE
=prompt VUPDATE is distributed under the MIT licence; its CA bundle under the MPL 2.0. Early test release.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [VUPDATE]README.VMS under the installation directory, and VUPDATE HELP.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for VUPDATE (vms-vupdate)
    At boot, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VUPDATE$STARTUP.COM
    For system managers, in their LOGIN.COM:
    $ @VUPDATE$ROOT:[COM]VUPDATE$SETUP.COM
    Then once per node: VUPDATE LOGIN. Optionally the nightly check:
    $ @VUPDATE$ROOT:[COM]VUPDATE_NIGHTLY START

PRODUCT REMOVE VUPDATE deletes the saved portal credentials, the cache and any
kept kits, stops the nightly check of the user removing it, and deassigns
VUPDATE$ROOT.
